# The nextpnr the gateware is placed and routed with (scripts/nextpnr.sh):
# the project's fork, built from source into .tools/nextpnr, used by
# rtl/Makefile in preference to the OSS CAD Suite's.
# Copyright © 2026 Thor H. Linløkken <thj@thj.no>
# License: CERN-OHL-S v2
#
# The fork carries Gowin timing the suite's nextpnr lacks: arcs for the
# DSP cells and the dual-port block RAM's port B address, and (with
# upstream since 2026-10-16) arcs for LUT1..LUT3 cells, a third of the
# LUTs of this design, which the pinned suite never timed. Measured on
# main (d03e915), one netlist, one seed, the boot self-test per clock
# step: the suite reports 119 MHz and the chip fails from 86; this
# nextpnr reports 82 and the chip holds to 110 (docs/gowin_oss_notes.md).
# The chip database is generated with the pack suite's Apicula, so the
# placement and the bitstream generator agree on the chip.
# The place-and-route result (rtl/Makefile: PLACER_BETA, SEED) belongs to
# this commit: change it by editing commit= (the full SHA, which is what
# git can fetch by) and running `make tools`.
repository=Thorwegian/nextpnr
commit=ddc708719e23ab41e3240c12b7d71a142f5ff1a6
